 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Bien que + subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "**Bien que** (although) is used with the subjunctive: **Bien que tu sois fatigué, tu viens** (although you are tired, you come).",
      "Another form: **quoique** (although), also with the subjunctive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Malgré + noun",
     "texto": [
      "**Malgré** (in spite of) goes with a noun, without a verb: **Malgré la pluie, je viens** (in spite of the rain, I'm coming)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pourtant, tout de même",
     "texto": [
      "**Pourtant** (however) and **tout de même** (all the same) go at the beginning or in the middle of the sentence: **Pourtant, il fait froid** (however, it is cold)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
